<title>USA: Venezuela to set $315 million 10-year Eurobond.</title>
<headline>Venezuela to set $315 million 10-year Eurobond.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Republic of Venezuela plans to set $315 million 10-year Eurobond via ING Barings, market sources said.</p>
<p>The deal is expected to price within the next couple of weeks, sources said.</p>
<p>Market speculation pegged the issue pricing inside of 300 basis points over comparable U.S. Treasuries.  Talk also circulated that the issue was &quot;heavily oversubscribed.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- Emerging Markets Desk, 212-859-1671))</p>
</text>
